{title: A Listening Heart}
{subtitle: 1 Kings 3:4–15}
{key: D}
{tempo: 88}
{time: 2/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [D] |
| [D] | [D] | [G] | [G] | ×2

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
At [D]Gibeon in the night the LORD [G]came in a dream
To a [D]young king newly crowned and not yet [A]sure of anything
[G]Ask what I should give you, said the LORD [D]to [A/C#]Solomon
[Bm]And the [G]king looked at his hands, still a [A]boy and not a man
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]You were kind to David, my [G]father, all his days
And you [D]set his son upon his throne to walk [A]in all his ways
But I am [G]only a young man, I don't know [D]how to go [A/C#]out or come [Bm]in
Among a [G]people so numerous they [A]cannot be counted in
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Give your [G]servant a listening [D]heart
To judge your [Bm]people
To discern be[A]tween good and evil
Not for [G]gold and not for [D]years
Give me [A]ears to [D]hear
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
It pleased the LORD that Solomon had asked [G]for this alone
Not for rich[D]es, not long life, not for en[A]emies overthrown
I [G]give you a heart so wise and dis[D]cerning, [A/C#]said the [Bm]LORD
And [G]what you did not ask for, riches [A]and honor, I will pour
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Give [G]your servant a listening [D]heart
To [Bm]judge your people
To discern [A]between good and evil
Not [G]for gold and not [D]for years
Give [A]me ears to [G]hear
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
